  "status": "experimental-public-api-not-conformance-evidence",
  "notes": "This contract records the portable C++ TCK check for the official IEEE 1516.1 timestamped ordinary attribute update surface across Flush Queue Request, Time Advance Request Available, Next Message Request Available, and Next Message Request. The source uses only the standard C++ RTIambassador and FederateAmbassador APIs plus the standard library; the adapter supplies the provider package, FOM, endpoint, callback configuration, and logical-time implementation. It verifies delivery and grant boundaries, then confirms that the early-NMR requester can send a timestamped attribute update at time seven after a grant at time five with lookahead one, without changing its logical time. It makes no provider-specific assertions.",
